  "gf_from_name": false,
  "second_half": "\\begin{remark}\nThe comment quoted in Section~1 chains two claims: the recurrence proved above, and the\nclosed form $a(n)=\\tfrac{529n}{2}-\\tfrac{529}{4}-\\tfrac{95(-1)^{n}}{4}$. The second holds\nas well, by the same generating function. Writing $\\theta=x\\frac{d}{dx}$, the sequence\n$n\\mapsto n$ has generating function $\\theta\\bigl[(1-x)^{-1}\\bigr]=x/(1-x)^{2}$ and\n$n\\mapsto(-1)^{n}$ has $1/(1+x)$, so the closed form has generating function\n\\[\n\\frac{529}{2}\\cdot\\frac{x}{(1-x)^{2}}-\\frac{529}{4}\\cdot\\frac{1}{1-x}\n-\\frac{95}{4}\\cdot\\frac{1}{1+x},\n\\]\nand subtracting \\eqref{eq:gf} this difference cancels identically to $0$. It was also\nchecked directly against all 40 published terms. Both halves of the comment therefore\nhold.\n\\end{remark}"
 }
